  "row_count": 21,
  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1687 K, melting point of Si; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 12.082$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.589 + 0.274 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.838 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.589\\times10^{-3}T+0.137\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.838\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.854$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1687 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 10.538 - 1.262 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{T} = 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 48.850 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 10.538 + 1.262 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 24.425 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 30.656 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1687-2000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -1.891 - 1.683 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.023 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 49.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -1.891 + 1.683 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.023 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 24.825 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 25.842 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Chase (19) who estimated some molecular constants. ",
    "lines_raw": [
      "Phase change: 1687 K, melting point of Si; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 12.082$ kcal/mol.",
      "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations:",
      "298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.589 + 0.274 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.838 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$",
      "$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.589\\times10^{-3}T+0.137\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.838\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.854$",
      "Reaction equations (kcal/mol):",
      "298.15-1687 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = 10.538 - 1.262 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{T} = 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 48.850 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 10.538 + 1.262 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.374 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} - 24.425 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 30.656 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "1687-2000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -1.891 - 1.683 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.023 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 49.650 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$",
      "$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -1.891 + 1.683 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.023 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 24.825 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 25.842 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$",
      "Source: Data from Chase (19) who estimated some molecular constants."
